  "description": "Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc WSD | 27.5\" women's mountain bike\nA great introduction to off-road cycling – the Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc WSD combines a lightweight alloy frame, front suspension and reliable disc brakes for exploring trails and enjoying everyday rides.\nThe Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc WSD is an entry-level women's mountain bike designed for riders looking to get started with trail riding and off-road adventures. Featuring a lightweight 6061 alloy frame with internal cable routing and 27.5\" wheels, it offers a versatile setup for exploring local trails, tackling uneven terrain and enjoying recreational cycling.\nAn 80mm suspension fork with lockout helps absorb bumps and uneven surfaces, providing added comfort and control when riding off-road. The 680mm alloy riser handlebars and Reid MTB grips offer a comfortable, confident steering position, while 2.1\" all-terrain MTB tyres provide reliable grip across trails, gravel paths and mixed surfaces.\nA 3x7-speed drivetrain, featuring Shimano Tourney front and TY300 rear derailleurs, provides 21 gearing options for tackling moderate inclines and enjoying everyday rides. Mechanical disc brakes with 160mm rotors deliver controlled stopping power in changing conditions, while double-wall alloy rims, a sealed bottom bracket and semi-integrated headset add durability for regular riding.\nFinished with a comfortable MTB saddle and practical components, the Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc WSD is a versatile choice for discovering local trails, exploring outdoor routes and enjoying weekend cycling.\nThe Reid Bikes MTB Sport Disc WSD is ideal for:\n\nWomen getting started with mountain biking, with a purpose-designed WSD frame and approachable entry-level setup\n\nTrail riding and outdoor adventures, with 80mm front suspension and lockout to help absorb bumps and uneven terrain\n\nEveryday recreational cycling, with a versatile setup for local paths and leisure rides\n\nRiders looking for versatile gearing, with a 3x7-speed drivetrain offering 21 gear options\n\nRiding across mixed surfaces, with 27.5\" wheels and 2.1\" all-terrain MTB tyres for grip and stability\n\nReliable stopping power, with mechanical disc brakes and 160mm rotors\n\nComfortable riding, with 680mm alloy riser handlebars, Reid MTB grips and an MTB comfort saddle",
